body:
### What happened?

The entire/checkpoints/v1 branch is never updated. I have only the initial commit.

When I make commits from claude code, my commit messages are appended with an entire checkpoint id

If I try to resume the branch I get: `Checkpoint '45b6a4757b39' found in commit but session metadata not available`

I see the postcommit and other hooks under .git/hooks and rerunning `entire enable` gives: `Already enabled. Everything looks good.`

If I try `entire doctor`, I get: `No stuck sessions found.`

If I look under `.entire/metadata/[sessionid]` I see a large `full.jsonl`, `prompt.txt`, and `summary.txt`

### Steps to reproduce

_No response_

### Entire CLI version

entire version Entire CLI 0.4.2 (2a9998e) Go version: go1.25.6 OS/Arch: darwin/arm64

### OS and architecture

Darwin 24.6.0 arm64

### Agent

Claude Code

### Strategy

manual-commit (default)

### Terminal

zsh

